  "author": "Blessing Effiong",
  "frontMatter": "A Love Written in Silence\nSome feelings are never spoken.\nSome love stories are never forgotten.\n❦\n\nBy Blessing Effiong\n\fCopyright\nA Love Written in Silence\n\nCopyright © 2026 by Blessing Effiong\n\nAll rights reserved.\n\nNo part of this publication may be reproduced, distributed, stored in a retrieval system, or transmitted\nin any form or by any means, electronic or mechanical, including photocopying, recording, or any\ninformation storage and retrieval system, without the prior written permission of the copyright holder,\nexcept for brief quotations used in reviews or other uses permitted by copyright law.\n\nFirst Edition\n\nPublished in 2026\n\nDisclaimer\n\nThis is a work of fiction. The names, characters, places, events, and dialogue in this book are\nproducts of the author's imagination or are used fictitiously. Any resemblance to actual persons, living\nor dead, businesses, organizations, events, or locales is entirely coincidental.\n\nWritten by\n\nBlessing Effiong\n\fDedication\nTo the ones who loved quietly.\n\nTo the hearts that smiled while breaking.\n\nTo the people who found comfort in books, silence, and the hope that tomorrow might bring\nsomething beautiful.\n\nTo those who waited, believed, and loved without expecting anything in return.\n\nAnd to anyone who has ever looked across a room, a classroom, or a library and wondered...\n\n\"What if?\"\n\nThis story is for you.\n\nWith love,\n\nBlessing Effiong\n\fIntroduction\nSome people fall in love with a single conversation.\n\nOthers fall in love with a smile.\n\nYoon-ah fell in love with the quiet moments.\n\nThe moments when no one was watching.\n\nThe moments that seemed ordinary to everyone else but meant everything to her.\n\nShe never planned to love him.\n\nShe never planned to write letters that carried pieces of her heart.\n\nAnd she certainly never imagined that the person she loved would treasure her words...\n\nwithout ever knowing they belonged to her.\n\nThis is not a story about perfect timing.\n\nIt is not a story about grand confessions or fairy-tale romance.\n\nIt is a story about the things left unsaid.\n\nAbout memories hidden between the pages of a book.\n\nAbout finding comfort in silence...\n\nand discovering that sometimes the loudest love is the one that is never spoken.\n\nSo, if you've ever loved someone quietly...\n\nIf you've ever smiled while hiding your tears...\n\nIf you've ever walked away carrying words you wished you had said...\n\nThen perhaps, somewhere in these pages...\n\nYou'll find a piece of yourself.\n\nTurn the page.\n\nSome stories don't begin with \"I love you.\"\n\nSome begin with silence.\n\f🎵 A Reading Playlist\nFor the best reading experience, find a quiet place, make yourself a warm drink, and\nlet soft music accompany this story.\n\nSuggested songs:\n\nSpring Day (Piano Version)\n\nLove Wins All (Piano Cover)\n\nPromise (Piano Instrumental)\n\nRiver Flows in You – Yiruma\n\nKiss the Rain – Yiruma\n\nAlways With Me (Piano Version)\n\nOne Summer's Day – Joe Hisaishi\n\nWind Forest – Joe Hisaishi\n\nNuvole Bianche – Ludovico Einaudi\n\nA Thousand Years (Piano Cover)\n\nReading Tip\n\n\n🌸\n\"There is no rush. Read slowly. Pause between chapters if you need to. Some stories are meant to be felt, not finished.\"\n\f📖 Table of Contents\n   Copyright\n   Dedication\n   Introduction\n   Reading Playlist\n\nChapters\n\n   Chapter 1 – The Boy at the Library\n   Chapter 2 – A Seat Beside You\n   Chapter 3 – The Quiet Afternoons\n   Chapter 4 – Between the Shelves\n   Chapter 5 – The Book I Didn't Mean to Borrow\n   Chapter 6 – Rain Against the Window\n   Chapter 7 – The Bookmark\n   Chapter 8 – The Smile I Waited For\n   Chapter 9 – A Cup of Hot Chocolate\n   Chapter 10 – The Way Home\n   Chapter 11 – The Little Things\n   Chapter 12 – Pages Filled with Silence\n   Chapter 13 – A Place Called Tomorrow\n   Chapter 14 – The Words I Never Said\n   Chapter 15 – The Letter I Couldn't Finish\n   Chapter 16 – Spring Begins\n   Chapter 17 – Cherry Blossoms\n   Chapter 18 – The Empty Seat\n   Chapter 19 – A Familiar Smile\n   Chapter 20 – Another Ordinary Day\n   Chapter 21 – The Library Card\n   Chapter 22 – The Sound of Turning Pages\n   Chapter 23 – A Promise Without Words\n   Chapter 24 – Waiting by the Window\n   Chapter 25 – The Afternoon Light\n   Chapter 26 – A Story Worth Remembering\n   Chapter 27 – The Quiet Between Us\n   Chapter 28 – The Place We Always Meet\n   Chapter 29 – The Bookmarks We Kept\n   Chapter 30 – A Heart Learning to Stay\n   Chapter 31 – The Season of Change\n\fChapter 32 – The Days That Mattered\nChapter 33 – The Road Back to You\nChapter 34 – Under the Cherry Blossoms\nChapter 35 – When I Started Looking for You\nChapter 36 – The Words I Couldn't Say\nChapter 37 – One More Day\nChapter 38 – The Days Between Us\nChapter 39 – Welcome Back\nChapter 40 – The Space Between Words\nChapter 41 – The Chair Across From Me\nChapter 42 – The Book I Couldn't Return\nChapter 43 – The Last Page\nChapter 44 – The Envelope in My Hands\nChapter 45 – The Letters We Never Meant to Keep\nChapter 46 – The Words Between the Lines\nChapter 47 – The Morning After\nChapter 48 – A Place Reserved for You\nChapter 49 – One Last Afternoon\nChapter 50 – A Love Written in Silence\nAcknowledgements\n\nAbout the Author\nThank You for Reading",
