      "number": 1,
      "content": "🌸Chapter 1\nThe Boy at the Library\n\nOpening Quote\n\n\"Some people enter your life with a conversation.\n\nOthers enter it with silence.\"\n\nThe library was never truly quiet.\n\nThere was always the soft sound of pages turning, chairs shifting, pens tapping against desks… life\nhappening in whispers.\n\nBut to Yoon-ah, it still felt like silence.\n\nShe liked sitting at the far corner near the window.\n\nNot because of the view.\n\nBut because no one looked at her there.\n\nExcept him.\n\nHe always arrived at the same time.\n\n2:14 PM.\n\nNever early. Never late.\n\nLike he had a reason to exist exactly at that moment.\n\nPark Jae-hyun didn’t walk into the library like most people did.\n\nHe entered like he already belonged there.\n\nOne hand holding books he never returned on time, the other slipping his bag off his shoulder like he\nhad done it a thousand times before.\n\nHe didn’t look around.\n\nHe never needed to.\n\nHe just walked straight to his seat.\n\nThe one near the window.\n\nThe one she secretly noticed every day.\n\nYoon-ah told herself she wasn’t watching him.\n\nShe was just… looking in that direction.\n\n\nAccidentally.\n\nRepeatedly.\n\nFor no reason at all.\n\nToday, something was different.\n\nHe didn’t sit immediately.\n\nInstead, he paused near the shelves.\n\nScanning.\n\nSearching.\n\nThen he reached for a book on the top shelf.\n\nToo high.\n\nHe stretched.\n\nThe book slipped.\n\nFell.\n\nRight onto her desk.\n\nFor a second, neither of them moved.\n\nThe sound of the book hitting the table felt too loud for a place like this.\n\nYoon-ah slowly looked up.\n\nAnd that was the first time their eyes met properly.\n\n“Oh,” he said softly.\n\nLike he was slightly embarrassed.\n\nNot awkward.\n\nJust human.\n\nHe bent down immediately, picking up the book from her desk.\n\n“Sorry,” he added. “Didn’t mean to interrupt your… whatever this is.”\n\nShe blinked.\n\n“…Studying,” she said quietly.\n\nHe smiled.\n\n\nThat easy smile again.\n\nLike it didn’t cost him anything.\n\nLike it came naturally.\n\n“Right,” he nodded. “Studying.”\n\nA pause.\n\nThen he held the book up slightly.\n\n“I needed this one for class. Literature analysis.”\n\nYoon-ah nodded again.\n\nShe didn’t know why her hands suddenly felt heavier.\n\nOr why her voice didn’t want to come out.\n\nHe turned slightly to leave, then stopped.\n\nLooked back at her desk.\n\n“You’re in Professor Kim’s class, right?”\n\nShe hesitated.\n\nThen nodded.\n\n“Yeah.”\n\nHe smiled again.\n\n“That class is brutal. Don’t miss tomorrow. He said something about a surprise quiz.”\n\nIt sounded like nothing.\n\nJust a normal sentence.\n\nA normal warning.\n\nA normal conversation between two students in a library.\n\nBut Yoon-ah remembered it.\n\nNot because it was important.\n\nBut because it was the first time he spoke to her like she existed.\n\n“Thanks,” she said quietly.\n\nHe gave a small wave.\n\n\n“See you around.”\n\nAnd then he walked away.\n\nBack to his seat.\n\nBack to his world.\n\nBack to the place where she didn’t exist yet.\n\nBut Yoon-ah stayed still for a long time.\n\nLooking at the space he had just stood in.\n\nAt the air he had just passed through.\n\nAt the moment that didn’t feel important to anyone else…\n\nbut felt like the beginning of everything to her.\n\nAnd for the first time that day, she didn’t open her book.\n\nShe just wrote one sentence in the margin of her notebook.\n\n “I think I just met someone I will never confess to.”\n\nEnding Quote\n\n\"The story hadn't begun with love.\n\nIt had begun with a glance.\""
