      "content": "🌸Chapter 10\nThe Coffee She Never Drank\n\nOpening Quote\n\n\"Kindness is dangerous...\n\nwhen your heart already belongs to someone.\"\n\nAutumn arrived quietly.\n\nThe leaves outside the library had begun to turn shades of gold and amber, covering the campus\npaths like forgotten memories.\n\nYoon-ah had always loved autumn.\n\nPeople said it was beautiful because everything changed.\n\nShe thought it was beautiful because everything learned how to let go.\n\nShe reached the library a few minutes before two.\n\nAs usual.\n\nShe placed her books on the table and looked toward the entrance.\n\n2:10 PM.\n\nNothing.\n\n2:13 PM.\n\nStill nothing.\n\nAt exactly 2:14...\n\nThe door opened.\n\nJae-hyun walked in, slightly out of breath.\n\nThe moment he saw her, he smiled.\n\n\"I made it.\"\n\nShe couldn't help smiling back.\n\n\"Barely.\"\n\nHe laughed.\n\n\"I know.\"\n\n\nIt was the first time she had ever teased him.\n\nIt was such a small moment...\n\nbut it stayed with both of them longer than either expected.\n\n\"I'll be right back,\" he said.\n\n\"I forgot something.\"\n\nBefore she could ask what it was, he disappeared again.\n\nA few minutes later, he returned carrying two paper cups.\n\nHe placed one gently in front of her.\n\n\"I noticed you always look sleepy in the afternoons.\"\n\n\"So...\"\n\n\"I bought you coffee.\"\n\nYoon-ah stared at the cup.\n\nHer hands didn't move.\n\nNo one had ever bought her coffee before.\n\nNot because they wanted something.\n\nNot because it was her birthday.\n\nJust because they noticed.\n\n\"I... I didn't bring any money.\"\n\nJae-hyun looked confused.\n\n\"What?\"\n\n\"I mean... I can pay you back tomorrow.\"\n\nHe laughed softly.\n\n\"It's just coffee.\"\n\nThen, after a pause, he added,\n\n\"You don't have to repay every act of kindness.\"\n\nShe looked down at the warm cup.\n\nThe heat seeped through the paper into her hands.\n\n\nFor some reason...\n\nit made her eyes sting.\n\n\"Thank you,\" she whispered.\n\n\"You're welcome.\"\n\nHe opened his notebook and started reading as if nothing unusual had happened.\n\nAs if he hadn't just given her something she would remember for years.\n\nShe took a small sip.\n\nIt was slightly bitter.\n\nSlightly sweet.\n\nShe wondered if love tasted the same.\n\nThat afternoon, Min-seo arrived carrying a stack of books.\n\n\"There you are!\"\n\nShe smiled brightly before sitting beside Jae-hyun.\n\n\"Oh!\"\n\nHer eyes landed on the second coffee cup.\n\n\"You bought Yoon-ah coffee?\"\n\nJae-hyun nodded casually.\n\n\"She always looks tired.\"\n\nMin-seo smiled.\n\n\"That's thoughtful.\"\n\nThen she turned toward Yoon-ah.\n\n\"You're lucky.\"\n\nYoon-ah forced a smile.\n\nLucky.\n\nIf only it were that simple.\n\nAn hour later, Jae-hyun received a phone call.\n\nHe apologized and stepped outside.\n\n\nThe moment he disappeared, Min-seo rested her chin on her hand.\n\n\"I think he's impossible not to like.\"\n\nYoon-ah's heart sank.\n\nMin-seo continued with a shy laugh.\n\n\"He notices little things.\"\n\n\"Like when someone's tired.\"\n\n\"Or when they're pretending to be okay.\"\n\nShe smiled to herself.\n\n\"I've never met someone like him.\"\n\nYoon-ah quietly wrapped both hands around the now-cold coffee cup.\n\nShe wanted to say,\n\n\"I know.\"\n\nInstead...\n\nshe simply nodded.\n\nWhen Jae-hyun returned, the conversation ended as naturally as it had begun.\n\nNone of them mentioned it again.\n\nBut the silence felt different.\n\nHe looked at the untouched half of Yoon-ah's coffee.\n\n\"Didn't like it?\"\n\nShe shook her head quickly.\n\n\"No...\"\n\nShe smiled softly.\n\n\"I just wanted it to last a little longer.\"\n\nHe chuckled, thinking she meant the drink.\n\nHe never imagined...\n\nshe meant the moment.\n\nThat night, Yoon-ah opened her notebook.\n\n\nInstead of writing a letter...\n\nshe stared at the coffee cup sitting on her desk.\n\nShe had washed it carefully.\n\nShe couldn't bring herself to throw it away.\n\nFinally, she picked up her pen.\n\nToday you bought me a cup of coffee.\n\nYou'll probably forget it by next week.\n\nBut I think... I'll remember it for the rest of my life.\n\nThat's the unfair thing about one-sided love.\n\nOne person's ordinary kindness becomes another person's unforgettable memory.\n\nShe folded the page.\n\nBut for the first time...\n\nshe didn't place it inside the novel.\n\nSome feelings...\n\nwere too precious to share.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n\"The coffee eventually grew cold.\n\nHer feelings never did.\""
