      "content": "🌸Chapter 11\nThe Empty Seat\n\nOpening Quote\n\n\"You never realize someone's place in your life...\n\nuntil it becomes empty.\"\n\nThe first sign that something was wrong...\n\nwas the empty chair.\n\n2:14 PM.\n\nThe library door opened.\n\nStudents came and went.\n\nThe chair across from Yoon-ah remained empty.\n\nShe glanced at the clock.\n\nMaybe he overslept.\n\nShe smiled to herself.\n\nIt wasn't impossible.\n\nJae-hyun had complained the day before about staying up all night to finish a design project.\n\nHe was probably exhausted.\n\nBy three o'clock...\n\nhe still hadn't come.\n\nShe opened her textbook.\n\nRead the same paragraph five times.\n\nCouldn't remember a single word.\n\nThe next day...\n\nthe chair was empty again.\n\n\"Have you seen Jae-hyun?\"\n\nMin-seo asked as she dropped into the seat beside Yoon-ah.\n\nYoon-ah shook her head.\n\n\n\"No.\"\n\n\"He isn't answering my messages either.\"\n\nFor the first time since they met...\n\nMin-seo looked worried.\n\nThree days passed.\n\nNo Jae-hyun.\n\nNo messages.\n\nNo letters read.\n\nThe novel remained untouched on the shelf.\n\nEach afternoon, Yoon-ah found herself staring at it.\n\nWaiting.\n\nHoping.\n\nLeaving the library disappointed.\n\nOn the fourth day...\n\nshe couldn't stop herself.\n\nAs she packed her books, she walked toward the librarian's desk.\n\n\"Excuse me...\"\n\nThe librarian looked up from a stack of returned books.\n\n\"Yes?\"\n\n\"I was wondering...\"\n\nShe hesitated.\n\n\"...Has Park Jae-hyun been here this week?\"\n\nThe librarian smiled apologetically.\n\n\"I'm afraid not.\"\n\n\"Oh.\"\n\n\"He usually greets me every afternoon.\"\n\n\"I noticed he hasn't been around.\"\n\n\n\"Maybe he's just busy.\"\n\nYoon-ah nodded politely.\n\nBut her heart refused to believe it.\n\nThat evening, rain began to fall.\n\nShe stood outside the university gate with her umbrella, watching students hurry home.\n\nThen she saw someone.\n\nMin-seo.\n\nStanding alone under a tree, staring at her phone.\n\nHer eyes were red.\n\nShe looked as though she had been crying.\n\nYoon-ah walked over carefully.\n\n\"Min-seo?\"\n\nShe looked up quickly, forcing a smile that didn't reach her eyes.\n\n\"Oh...\"\n\n\"It's you.\"\n\n\"Is everything okay?\"\n\nMin-seo lowered her head.\n\n\"My grandmother...\"\n\n\"She collapsed three days ago.\"\n\nYoon-ah's heart tightened.\n\n\"Jae-hyun has been at the hospital with her.\"\n\n\"He practically grew up with her.\"\n\n\"I think...\"\n\nShe paused.\n\n\"...I think he's forgotten the rest of the world.\"\n\nThat night...\n\nYoon-ah couldn't sleep.\n\n\nShe imagined him sitting in a hospital corridor.\n\nStill wearing the same tired smile.\n\nTrying to be strong for everyone else.\n\nWho was taking care of him?\n\nWho was asking if he had eaten?\n\nWho was reminding him to rest?\n\nProbably no one.\n\nThe next afternoon...\n\ninstead of going to the library immediately...\n\nYoon-ah stopped at a small bakery near the hospital.\n\nShe bought warm bread.\n\nA bottle of water.\n\nAnd a small carton of banana milk.\n\nShe remembered him mentioning once that he liked it.\n\nIt had been such a casual comment.\n\nMonths ago.\n\nShe had remembered anyway.\n\nShe stood outside the hospital entrance for nearly ten minutes.\n\nThe bag felt heavier with every passing second.\n\nWhat am I doing?\n\nHe didn't ask me to come.\n\nHe might think this is strange.\n\nJust as she was about to turn around and leave...\n\nthe hospital doors opened.\n\nJae-hyun stepped outside.\n\nHis shoulders looked heavier.\n\nHis eyes were tired.\n\n\nHe hadn't noticed her yet.\n\nHe leaned against the wall and closed his eyes for a moment.\n\nAs if he had forgotten how exhausting it was to simply exist.\n\nYoon-ah took one small step forward.\n\nThen another.\n\nBefore she could lose her courage...\n\nshe held out the paper bag.\n\n\"...You should eat something.\"\n\nJae-hyun looked up in surprise.\n\nFor a long moment...\n\nhe simply stared at her.\n\nThen at the bag.\n\nThen back at her.\n\n\"You came all the way here?\"\n\nShe nodded.\n\n\"I heard...\"\n\n\"...about your grandmother.\"\n\nSilence settled between them.\n\nNot awkward.\n\nJust gentle.\n\nFinally, he accepted the bag with both hands.\n\n\"Thank you.\"\n\nHis voice was quieter than usual.\n\n\"I didn't realize how hungry I was.\"\n\nYoon-ah smiled softly.\n\n\"I'm glad.\"\n\nHe looked at the contents of the bag.\n\n\nBread.\n\nWater.\n\nBanana milk.\n\nHe blinked.\n\n\"...How did you know this is my favorite?\"\n\nYoon-ah's heart skipped.\n\nShe hadn't planned an answer.\n\n\"I...\"\n\nShe looked down.\n\n\"I remembered.\"\n\nJae-hyun smiled.\n\nA tired...\n\ngrateful...\n\nbeautiful smile.\n\n\"I guess...\"\n\nhe said quietly,\n\n\"...you notice little things too.\"\n\nFor the first time...\n\nhe wasn't talking about the mysterious letters.\n\nHe was talking about her.\n\nAnd somehow...\n\nthose words meant even more.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n\"Sometimes love isn't saying, 'I miss you.'\n\nSometimes it's simply bringing someone something to eat.\""
