      "number": 12,
      "content": "🌸Chapter 12\nThe Scarf\n\nOpening Quote\n\n\"Warmth isn't always found in winter.\n\nSometimes it's found in people.\"\n\nThe first cold wind of winter arrived two weeks later.\n\nStudents walked across campus with their hands tucked into their coat pockets, their breaths\ndisappearing into the morning air.\n\nYoon-ah pulled her cardigan tighter around herself as she hurried toward the library.\n\nShe had forgotten her scarf.\n\nAgain.\n\nWhen she pushed open the library door, warm air greeted her.\n\nSo did Jae-hyun.\n\nHe was already sitting at their table, reading.\n\nWhen he looked up, he frowned slightly.\n\n\"You're freezing.\"\n\n\"I'm okay.\"\n\n\"You don't look okay.\"\n\nShe laughed softly.\n\n\"I forgot my scarf.\"\n\nHe glanced at the empty chair beside him.\n\nThen, without another word, he stood up.\n\nBefore Yoon-ah could ask what he was doing...\n\nhe untied the dark blue scarf around his own neck.\n\nShe looked at him in confusion.\n\n\"What are you doing?\"\n\n\"You'll catch a cold.\"\n\n\n\"It's fine.\"\n\n\"It isn't.\"\n\nHe stepped closer.\n\n\"May I?\"\n\nYoon-ah couldn't speak.\n\nShe only nodded.\n\nVery gently...\n\nhe wrapped the scarf around her neck.\n\nHis fingers brushed against the ends of her hair as he adjusted it.\n\nThe moment lasted only a few seconds.\n\nBut to Yoon-ah...\n\nthe entire world had gone still.\n\n\"There.\"\n\nHe stepped back, smiling.\n\n\"Better.\"\n\nShe touched the soft fabric around her neck.\n\n\"It belongs to you.\"\n\n\"You can give it back tomorrow.\"\n\nHis smile widened.\n\n\"Unless you plan on stealing it.\"\n\nShe laughed.\n\nA real laugh.\n\nThe kind that escaped before she could stop it.\n\nJae-hyun looked at her for a moment.\n\nThen smiled to himself.\n\n\"I think that's the first time I've heard you laugh like that.\"\n\nYoon-ah's cheeks warmed.\n\n\n\"I guess...\"\n\nshe said quietly,\n\n\"...I forgot how.\"\n\nFor a brief moment, neither of them spoke.\n\nThe silence between them wasn't uncomfortable.\n\nIt felt... peaceful.\n\nLike two people who didn't need many words to understand each other.\n\nThe peace didn't last.\n\nThe library doors opened.\n\n\"Jae-hyun!\"\n\nMin-seo walked in carrying a shopping bag.\n\nShe stopped the moment she saw Yoon-ah wearing the scarf.\n\n\"Oh.\"\n\nHer smile faltered for just a second.\n\n\"You finally gave it away.\"\n\nJae-hyun blinked.\n\n\"What?\"\n\n\"The scarf.\"\n\n\"You've had it since high school.\"\n\n\"You never let anyone borrow it.\"\n\nShe laughed awkwardly.\n\n\"I remember asking once, and you said no.\"\n\nThe room suddenly felt smaller.\n\nYoon-ah instinctively reached for the scarf.\n\n\"I should take it off.\"\n\n\"No.\"\n\nJae-hyun answered a little too quickly.\n\n\nBoth girls looked at him.\n\nHe cleared his throat.\n\n\"I mean...\"\n\n\"...it's cold.\"\n\n\"You can keep wearing it today.\"\n\nMin-seo smiled politely.\n\n\"That's sweet.\"\n\nBut there was something unreadable in her eyes.\n\nSomething that hadn't been there before.\n\nThe rest of the afternoon passed quietly.\n\nYet something had changed.\n\nNot between Yoon-ah and Jae-hyun.\n\nBetween everyone.\n\nFor the first time...\n\nMin-seo noticed that Jae-hyun looked at Yoon-ah differently.\n\nNot romantically.\n\nNot yet.\n\nBut with a comfort he didn't seem to share with anyone else.\n\nThat evening, as they packed their bags, Yoon-ah carefully folded the scarf.\n\nShe held it out to him.\n\n\"Thank you.\"\n\nHe looked at it.\n\nThen back at her.\n\n\"You can keep it until tomorrow.\"\n\nShe smiled.\n\n\"I'll bring it.\"\n\n\"I know you will.\"\n\n\nTheir eyes met.\n\nJust for a second.\n\nLong enough for something unspoken to pass between them.\n\nOn the way home, Jae-hyun reached into his backpack to put away a notebook.\n\nThe stack of anonymous letters slipped out.\n\nOne page unfolded across his lap.\n\nHis eyes landed on a sentence he had read many times before.\n\n\"Sometimes, being remembered feels warmer than wearing a coat in winter.\"\n\nHe frowned slightly.\n\nThen looked out the bus window.\n\nWithout realizing it...\n\nhe whispered,\n\n\"Why does that remind me of Yoon-ah?\"\n\nThe bus continued through the falling snow.\n\nAnd for the very first time...\n\nthe girl behind the letters and the girl sitting across from him...\n\nbegan to feel like they might be the same person.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n\"Some scarves keep away the cold.\n\nOthers keep a memory alive.\""
