      "number": 13,
      "content": "🌸Chapter 13\nAlmost\n\nOpening Quote\n\n\"The truth has a strange way of finding those who seek it.\"\n\nThe scarf still smelled faintly of him.\n\nYoon-ah noticed it the moment she hung it by her bedroom window.\n\nIt carried the clean scent of laundry, mixed with something she couldn't describe.\n\nShe told herself she should wash it before returning it.\n\nInstead...\n\nshe simply looked at it.\n\nThe next morning, she folded it neatly into a paper bag.\n\nShe tied the handles carefully, as if protecting something fragile.\n\nNot the scarf.\n\nThe memory.\n\nWhen she arrived at the library, Jae-hyun wasn't there yet.\n\nHis chair sat empty.\n\nThe paper bag rested on the table beside her books.\n\nShe kept glancing at it every few minutes.\n\nWhy was she nervous?\n\nShe was only returning something that belonged to him.\n\nNothing more.\n\nAt exactly 2:14 p.m., the library door opened.\n\n\"There you are,\" Jae-hyun said with a smile.\n\n\"I thought I'd be late.\"\n\nHe took his usual seat.\n\nThen noticed the paper bag.\n\n\"My scarf.\"\n\n\nYoon-ah nodded.\n\n\"I washed it.\"\n\n\"You didn't have to.\"\n\n\"I wanted to.\"\n\nHe reached inside the bag.\n\nFor a moment, his fingers paused.\n\nThere was something else inside.\n\nA small packet of honey candies.\n\nHis favorite.\n\nHe looked up.\n\n\"You bought these?\"\n\nYoon-ah blinked.\n\n\"Oh...\"\n\n\"I remembered you said they help when your throat hurts.\"\n\nHe stared at her.\n\n\"I only mentioned that once.\"\n\nShe smiled shyly.\n\n\"You did.\"\n\nFor a few seconds, neither of them spoke.\n\nA strange feeling settled over him.\n\nShe remembered things.\n\nSmall things.\n\nTiny details most people forgot within minutes.\n\nJust like...\n\nThe letters.\n\nHe quietly reached into his backpack.\n\nThe folded pages were still there.\n\n\nHe opened one.\n\nHis eyes stopped on a familiar sentence.\n\n\"People don't fall in love because of grand gestures.\n\nSometimes... it begins because someone remembers the little things everyone else forgets.\"\n\nHis heart skipped.\n\nHe looked up at Yoon-ah.\n\nShe was reading peacefully, unaware that he was watching her.\n\nOr perhaps...\n\npretending not to notice.\n\nCould it be...?\n\nThe thought came suddenly.\n\nWithout permission.\n\nWithout reason.\n\nHe almost laughed at himself.\n\nNo.\n\nIt couldn't be.\n\nThere were thousands of students at the university.\n\nWhy would it be her?\n\nStill...\n\nThe thought refused to leave.\n\nLater that afternoon, Min-seo hurried into the library, cheeks flushed from the cold.\n\n\"I finally finished my project!\" she announced.\n\nJae-hyun smiled.\n\n\"Congratulations.\"\n\nShe placed three cups of hot chocolate on the table.\n\n\"One for each of us.\"\n\nYoon-ah looked surprised.\n\n\n\"You didn't have to.\"\n\n\"I wanted to.\"\n\nThey spent the next hour talking about classes, professors, and the upcoming winter festival.\n\nIt was the longest conversation the three of them had ever shared.\n\nFor a little while...\n\neverything felt normal.\n\nAs the sun began to set, Min-seo suddenly turned to Yoon-ah.\n\n\"I've always wanted to ask you something.\"\n\nYoon-ah looked up.\n\n\"You write, don't you?\"\n\nHer heart nearly stopped.\n\n\"I've seen your notebook.\"\n\n\"The way you write...\"\n\nMin-seo smiled warmly.\n\n\"It feels like reading a novel.\"\n\nJae-hyun looked toward Yoon-ah.\n\nInterested.\n\nShe lowered her eyes.\n\n\"It's nothing.\"\n\n\"I just write when I can't sleep.\"\n\nMin-seo laughed.\n\n\"Then one day you should let us read it.\"\n\nYoon-ah smiled politely.\n\n\"Maybe someday.\"\n\nBut inside, she whispered:\n\nI hope that day never comes.\n\nThat evening, after everyone left, Jae-hyun stayed behind.\n\n\nHe walked to the shelf.\n\nPulled out the familiar novel.\n\nNo letter.\n\nHe checked again.\n\nNothing.\n\nFor the first time in months...\n\nthere was no folded page waiting for him.\n\nHe stood there longer than he meant to.\n\nThen, almost without thinking, he said quietly,\n\n\"I hope you're okay.\"\n\nHe wasn't sure whether he was talking to the anonymous writer...\n\nor to the girl who had remembered his favorite candies.\n\nAnd somehow...\n\nthat frightened him.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n\"He almost knew.\n\nShe almost told him.\n\nAlmost... became its own kind of heartbreak.\""
