      "content": "🌸Chapter 14\nThe Song She Never Knew\n\nOpening Quote\n\n\"Sometimes love is learning someone else's favorite song...\n\nbefore they ever ask you to listen.\"\n\nWinter settled over the campus like a quiet promise.\n\nThe trees stood bare.\n\nThe mornings arrived wrapped in pale fog.\n\nAnd every afternoon...\n\nat exactly 2:14 p.m...\n\nJae-hyun still walked through the library doors.\n\nSome things never changed.\n\nAnd somehow...\n\nthat comforted Yoon-ah.\n\nThe anonymous letters had stopped.\n\nIt had been twelve days.\n\nTwelve afternoons.\n\nTwelve empty pages.\n\nJae-hyun never mentioned them.\n\nBut every time he borrowed the old novel, he still opened it.\n\nJust in case.\n\nEvery time...\n\nhe found nothing.\n\nOne afternoon, the silence between them stretched longer than usual.\n\nJae-hyun closed his textbook with a sigh.\n\n\"I can't concentrate.\"\n\nYoon-ah looked up.\n\n\n\"Tired?\"\n\n\"A little.\"\n\nHe rubbed the back of his neck.\n\n\"My design project is due next week.\"\n\n\"You'll do well.\"\n\nHe smiled.\n\n\"You sound very confident.\"\n\n\"I am.\"\n\n\"Why?\"\n\nShe lowered her eyes.\n\n\"Because...\"\n\n\"...you always finish what you start.\"\n\nFor a second...\n\nhe simply looked at her.\n\nThen he laughed quietly.\n\n\"I wish I believed in myself the way you do.\"\n\nLater that afternoon, the library speakers came to life.\n\nA soft piano melody filled the room.\n\nIt wasn't loud.\n\nJust enough to drift between the bookshelves.\n\nJae-hyun stopped writing.\n\n\"I know this song.\"\n\n\"You do?\"\n\n\"My grandmother used to play it every Sunday morning.\"\n\nHe smiled at the memory.\n\n\"I haven't heard it in years.\"\n\nYoon-ah listened carefully.\n\n\nShe had never heard it before.\n\nBut from the way his eyes softened...\n\nshe knew it must have meant something.\n\nAfter leaving the library that evening, she walked into a small music shop near the bus stop.\n\n\"Excuse me,\" she asked the elderly shopkeeper.\n\n\"The song that played on the university radio today...\"\n\nHe smiled.\n\n\"If you hum it, I'll try.\"\n\nEmbarrassed, she quietly hummed the melody.\n\nThe old man nodded almost immediately.\n\n\"Ah.\"\n\n\"I know exactly which one.\"\n\nHe wrote the title on a small piece of paper and handed it to her.\n\n\"Beautiful choice.\"\n\nShe smiled.\n\n\"Thank you.\"\n\nThat night...\n\nshe played the melody over and over again.\n\nNot because she loved it.\n\nBecause...\n\nhe did.\n\nShe imagined his grandmother sitting at an old piano.\n\nShe imagined a younger Jae-hyun listening from the hallway.\n\nShe imagined memories she had never lived.\n\nYet somehow...\n\nthey made her smile.\n\nThe next afternoon...\n\n\nJae-hyun arrived looking unusually exhausted.\n\nBefore he even sat down...\n\nYoon-ah slid a small envelope across the table.\n\nHe looked confused.\n\n\"What's this?\"\n\n\"Open it later.\"\n\nHe blinked.\n\n\"For me?\"\n\nShe nodded once.\n\nWhen he finally opened it during a break...\n\nhe found a handwritten note.\n\nIt wasn't a letter.\n\nJust one sentence.\n\nAlong with a tiny music card.\n\n\"Some memories deserve to be heard again.\"\n\nHis eyes widened.\n\nIt was the same piano piece.\n\nThe one his grandmother loved.\n\nHe looked across the table.\n\n\"How did you...?\"\n\nYoon-ah smiled softly.\n\n\"I asked around.\"\n\n\"You remembered.\"\n\nShe nodded.\n\n\"You looked happy when you talked about it.\"\n\nFor a long moment...\n\nJae-hyun couldn't find any words.\n\n\nHe had never told anyone how much that song meant to him.\n\nNot even Min-seo.\n\nYet somehow...\n\nYoon-ah had quietly carried that memory for him.\n\nWithout being asked.\n\nWithout expecting anything in return.\n\nAs they packed up to leave, Jae-hyun spoke almost absentmindedly.\n\n\"You know...\"\n\nShe looked at him.\n\n\"Sometimes...\"\n\nhe smiled to himself.\n\n\"...I feel like you've known me much longer than we actually have.\"\n\nYoon-ah's heart skipped.\n\nIf only he knew.\n\nThat evening, Jae-hyun sat alone in his room.\n\nThe music played softly through his headphones.\n\nHis eyes drifted toward the folder where he kept the anonymous letters.\n\nWithout thinking...\n\nhe took one out.\n\nHis gaze landed on a familiar sentence.\n\n\"Love is remembering the smallest pieces of someone, even when they forget they ever shared them.\"\n\nHe read it once.\n\nThen looked at the music card Yoon-ah had given him.\n\nThe handwriting...\n\nThe gentle choice of words...\n\nThe quiet way both gifts made him feel...\n\nHe frowned.\n\n\nNot in confusion.\n\nIn recognition.\n\nA thought returned to him.\n\nThe same thought he had pushed away before.\n\nThis time...\n\nit stayed.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n\"Memories become music.\n\nAnd music remembers what hearts cannot forget.\""
