      "content": "❄️Chapter 15\nSnowfall\n\nOpening Quote\n\n\"The first snowfall never lasts forever.\n\nBut the memory of who stood beside you often does.\"\n\nThe first snow arrived without warning.\n\nIt wasn't heavy.\n\nJust tiny white flakes drifting through the afternoon sky, settling gently on rooftops, tree branches, and\nthe quiet paths around the university.\n\nStudents gathered outside, pointing toward the sky with childlike excitement.\n\n\"It's snowing!\"\n\nYoon-ah stopped walking.\n\nShe stretched out her hand.\n\nA single snowflake landed on her glove...\n\nand disappeared almost immediately.\n\nShe smiled.\n\n\"So this is what first snow feels like...\"\n\nshe whispered.\n\n\"There you are.\"\n\nJae-hyun's voice came from behind her.\n\nShe turned.\n\nHe stood a few steps away, his hands buried in the pockets of his dark coat.\n\n\"You'll be late for the library.\"\n\n\"I know.\"\n\n\"But...\"\n\nShe looked back at the falling snow.\n\n\"I've never seen snow before.\"\n\n\nJae-hyun looked up.\n\nNeither had he.\n\nNot like this.\n\nNot in person.\n\nFor a moment...\n\nthey simply stood there.\n\nWatching the sky.\n\nWithout saying anything.\n\n\"They say...\"\n\nJae-hyun began quietly.\n\n\"...that if you see the first snowfall with someone important...\"\n\nHe stopped.\n\nYoon-ah looked at him.\n\n\"...what happens?\"\n\nHe laughed softly.\n\n\"I don't remember.\"\n\n\"You forgot?\"\n\n\"I was hoping you'd know.\"\n\nShe smiled.\n\n\"I don't.\"\n\n\"Then...\"\n\nhe shrugged.\n\n\"...let's make up our own meaning.\"\n\nThe two of them walked toward the library together.\n\nThe campus seemed quieter than usual.\n\nThe snow softened every sound.\n\nEven their footsteps felt lighter.\n\n\nInside the library, the windows slowly fogged over from the warmth.\n\nJae-hyun rubbed the glass with his sleeve and drew a tiny snowflake with his finger.\n\n\"It's already melting.\"\n\n\"Everything does.\"\n\nYoon-ah answered before thinking.\n\nHe looked at her.\n\nShe quickly lowered her eyes.\n\n\"I mean...\"\n\n\"...snow.\"\n\nHe smiled.\n\n\"I know what you meant.\"\n\nThe afternoon passed peacefully.\n\nNeither of them spoke much.\n\nSometimes silence didn't need to be filled.\n\nSometimes...\n\nit was enough.\n\nAs the library prepared to close, students hurried outside.\n\nThe snowfall had grown heavier.\n\nJae-hyun stood by the entrance, looking at the sky.\n\n\"You brought an umbrella?\"\n\nYoon-ah nodded.\n\n\"One.\"\n\n\"So did I.\"\n\nThey looked at each other.\n\nThen laughed.\n\n\"I guess...\"\n\nhe said,\n\n\n\"...we'll both get home dry.\"\n\nOutside the library gates, they reached the familiar crossroads where they always parted.\n\nYoon-ah stopped.\n\n\"So...\"\n\n\"I'll see you tomorrow.\"\n\nJae-hyun nodded.\n\n\"Tomorrow.\"\n\nNeither of them moved.\n\nFor the first time...\n\ngoing in opposite directions felt strangely difficult.\n\nJust then, a little girl ran past them, chasing snowflakes with her older brother.\n\nShe slipped.\n\nBefore she could fall, her brother caught her hand.\n\n\"It's okay.\"\n\n\"I'm here.\"\n\nThe little girl laughed as though nothing had happened.\n\nYoon-ah watched them disappear down the street.\n\nWithout realizing it...\n\nshe whispered,\n\n\"They're lucky.\"\n\nJae-hyun heard her.\n\n\"They are.\"\n\n\"What do you think love looks like?\"\n\nThe question escaped him before he could stop it.\n\nYoon-ah looked surprised.\n\n\"I don't know.\"\n\nShe thought for a moment.\n\n\nThen answered honestly.\n\n\"I think...\"\n\n\"...love is remembering someone when they're not with you.\"\n\nJae-hyun didn't respond immediately.\n\nInstead...\n\nhe looked at the falling snow.\n\nBecause for some reason...\n\nher answer reminded him of the anonymous letters.\n\nThat night, Yoon-ah sat at her desk.\n\nThe old notebook lay open before her.\n\nShe hadn't written another anonymous letter in weeks.\n\nShe told herself she had stopped.\n\nThat it was over.\n\nBut tonight...\n\nthe words returned.\n\nShe picked up her pen.\n\nSlowly...\n\ncarefully...\n\nshe began to write.\n\nToday we watched the first snowfall together.\n\nYou probably won't remember every detail.\n\nBut I will.\n\nYears from now, if someone asks me when winter became my favorite season...\n\nI'll remember today.\n\nNot because it snowed.\n\nBut because you were standing beside me when it did.\n\nShe stared at the page for a long time.\n\n\nThen folded it.\n\nBut instead of placing it inside the familiar library novel...\n\nshe tucked it between the pages of her own notebook.\n\nSome memories...\n\nshe wanted to keep for herself.\n\nFar away, in his room...\n\nJae-hyun looked out the window as snow continued to fall.\n\nFor reasons he couldn't explain...\n\nhe found himself wondering what Yoon-ah was doing at that exact moment.\n\nIt was a simple thought.\n\nA passing thought.\n\nYet it stayed with him longer than it should have.\n\nOutside...\n\nthe snow covered the world in white.\n\nInside...\n\nsomething quiet had begun to change.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n\"Winter covered the world in white.\n\nTheir hearts remained full of words left unspoken.\""
