      "content": "🌸Chapter 16\nThe Forgotten Bookmark\n\nOpening Quote\n\n\"Sometimes the smallest things are the ones that lead us to the biggest truths.\"\n\nThe snowfall had stopped.\n\nMorning sunlight reflected off the thin layer of white that still covered the campus.\n\nEverything looked brighter.\n\nQuieter.\n\nAs if winter itself had paused to listen.\n\nYoon-ah arrived at the library with a book tucked against her chest.\n\nShe smiled politely at the librarian before making her way to the familiar table by the window.\n\nFor the first time in weeks...\n\nShe arrived before Jae-hyun.\n\nShe opened her notebook.\n\nHer pen hovered over the page.\n\nBut no words came.\n\nInstead...\n\nShe found herself smiling.\n\nYesterday's snowfall lingered in her mind.\n\nNot because of the snow.\n\nBecause of him.\n\nAt exactly 2:14 p.m...\n\nThe library door opened.\n\nJae-hyun stepped inside, brushing a few snowflakes from his coat.\n\nWhen he saw her already sitting there...\n\nHe smiled.\n\n\"I thought I'd be the first one here.\"\n\n\n\"You almost were.\"\n\nHe laughed.\n\n\"I'll take almost.\"\n\nThe afternoon passed in peaceful silence.\n\nThe kind that no longer felt awkward.\n\nEvery now and then...\n\nOne of them would glance up.\n\nOnly to discover the other had done the same.\n\nThey would quickly return to their books...\n\nPretending nothing had happened.\n\nA few hours later...\n\nJae-hyun stood up.\n\n\"I'll be back.\"\n\nHe disappeared between the bookshelves.\n\nYoon-ah continued reading.\n\nOr at least...\n\nShe tried to.\n\nWhen he returned, he was carrying three books.\n\nAs he placed them on the table...\n\nA small bookmark slipped from one of them.\n\nNeither of them noticed.\n\nThey packed their bags as the library announced its closing time.\n\nAfter saying goodbye...\n\nJae-hyun hurried outside.\n\nHe was halfway across the courtyard when he reached into his book.\n\nHis bookmark was gone.\n\nBack inside...\n\n\nYoon-ah noticed something lying beside her chair.\n\nA bookmark.\n\nShe picked it up.\n\nIt was handmade.\n\nSimple.\n\nPressed between the clear plastic was a tiny dried cherry blossom.\n\nAt the bottom, written in neat handwriting, were the words:\n\n\"Some pages deserve to be remembered.\"\n\nShe smiled.\n\n\"It sounds like something he would write.\"\n\nThe next afternoon...\n\nJae-hyun looked unusually distracted.\n\n\"You lost something?\"\n\nYoon-ah asked quietly.\n\nHe looked surprised.\n\n\"My bookmark.\"\n\n\"It belonged to my grandmother.\"\n\n\"I've had it since I was little.\"\n\n\"I looked everywhere.\"\n\n\"I guess it's gone.\"\n\nHe tried to smile.\n\n\"But it's okay.\"\n\nSomehow...\n\nHis smile looked sad.\n\nYoon-ah reached into her bag.\n\nWithout saying a word...\n\nShe placed the bookmark on the table.\n\n\nHis eyes widened.\n\n\"You found it?\"\n\nShe nodded.\n\n\"It was beside my chair yesterday.\"\n\nFor a moment...\n\nHe simply stared at it.\n\nThen at her.\n\nThen back at the bookmark.\n\nRelief spread across his face.\n\n\"You have no idea how much this means to me.\"\n\nHis voice was barely above a whisper.\n\n\"I thought I'd lost the last thing my grandmother made for me.\"\n\nYoon-ah smiled softly.\n\n\"I'm glad it found its way back.\"\n\nHe carefully slipped the bookmark between the pages of his novel.\n\nHis fingers lingered on the dried blossom.\n\n\"You know...\"\n\nHe looked at her.\n\n\"You've been returning a lot of things to me lately.\"\n\n\"My scarf.\"\n\n\"My favorite music.\"\n\n\"My bookmark.\"\n\nHe laughed quietly.\n\n\"I wonder what I'd lose without you around.\"\n\nThe words escaped before he could think.\n\nYoon-ah's heart skipped.\n\nHe froze.\n\n\nRealizing what he had said.\n\n\"I...\"\n\nHe rubbed the back of his neck awkwardly.\n\n\"I didn't mean...\"\n\nShe smiled.\n\n\"I know.\"\n\nBut somehow...\n\nNeither of them believed that anymore.\n\nThat evening...\n\nAs Jae-hyun opened the old novel containing the anonymous letters...\n\nThe bookmark rested quietly between its pages.\n\nHis eyes drifted to the stack of letters in his drawer.\n\nThen back to the bookmark.\n\nThen to the empty chair across from him in his memory.\n\nA strange feeling settled in his heart.\n\nNot certainty.\n\nNot confusion.\n\nSomething in between.\n\nThe kind of feeling that quietly changes everything...\n\nLong before anyone notices.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n\"Sometimes we spend so long searching for what we've lost...\n\nonly to discover it was quietly waiting beside us all along.\""
