      "number": 17,
      "content": "🌸Chapter 17\nThe Umbrella\n\nOpening Quote\n\n“The heart doesn't always notice the moment it begins to change.\n\nSometimes... everyone else notices first.”\n\nRain arrived without warning.\n\nOne moment, the sky was clear.\n\nThe next...\n\nthe campus disappeared beneath a curtain of falling rain.\n\nStudents rushed toward the nearest buildings, laughing as they tried to avoid getting soaked.\n\nYoon-ah stood beneath the library steps.\n\nShe opened her umbrella.\n\nIt was small.\n\nBarely enough for one person.\n\n\"You brought one too?\"\n\nShe turned.\n\nJae-hyun stood beside her.\n\nHis umbrella was nowhere to be seen.\n\n\"I thought I did.\"\n\nHe searched through his backpack again.\n\nThen laughed.\n\n\"I guess I left it at home.\"\n\n\"You can borrow mine.\"\n\nHe shook his head.\n\n\"And leave you standing here?\"\n\n\"I'm okay.\"\n\n\"So am I.\"\n\n\nThe rain grew heavier.\n\nNeither of them moved.\n\nA familiar voice interrupted them.\n\n\"Jae-hyun!\"\n\nMin-seo came running across the courtyard.\n\nShe held a large umbrella above her head.\n\n\"I brought this for you.\"\n\nShe smiled brightly.\n\n\"I checked the weather this morning.\"\n\nJae-hyun blinked in surprise.\n\n\"You walked all the way here?\"\n\nShe nodded.\n\n\"I didn't want you getting caught in the rain.\"\n\nFor a brief moment...\n\nthe three of them stood together beneath the gray sky.\n\nYoon-ah smiled politely.\n\n\"You should go.\"\n\nJae-hyun looked from Min-seo...\n\nto Yoon-ah.\n\nThen back again.\n\n\"What about you?\"\n\n\"I'll wait.\"\n\n\"It's fine.\"\n\n\"I like the rain.\"\n\nIt wasn't true.\n\nBut it was easier than saying,\n\n\"I don't want to be the reason someone gets hurt.\"\n\n\nJae-hyun hesitated.\n\nSomething about leaving Yoon-ah alone didn't feel right.\n\nBefore he could speak...\n\nYoon-ah gently stepped back.\n\n\"I'll see you tomorrow.\"\n\nShe smiled.\n\nThe same quiet smile she always wore.\n\nThen she opened her umbrella and walked into the rain.\n\nJae-hyun watched her disappear.\n\nHe didn't know why...\n\nbut seeing her walk away made his chest feel strangely heavy.\n\n\"You seem worried.\"\n\nMin-seo's voice was soft.\n\nHe looked away.\n\n\"I just hope she gets home safely.\"\n\nMin-seo lowered her eyes.\n\n\"So do I.\"\n\nThat evening...\n\nthe rain continued.\n\nYoon-ah arrived home with damp sleeves despite the umbrella.\n\nShe changed into warm clothes and sat by her bedroom window.\n\nRaindrops traced quiet paths down the glass.\n\nShe smiled to herself.\n\nToday hadn't gone the way she'd imagined.\n\nBut somehow...\n\nshe wasn't upset.\n\nBecause love had never been about being chosen.\n\n\nNot for her.\n\nIt had always been about quietly wishing for someone else's happiness.\n\nEven if it meant walking home alone.\n\nThe next afternoon...\n\nJae-hyun arrived at the library carrying a neatly folded umbrella.\n\nHe placed it on the table.\n\nYoon-ah looked confused.\n\n\"What's this?\"\n\n\"For you.\"\n\nShe blinked.\n\n\"I already have one.\"\n\n\"I know.\"\n\nHe smiled.\n\n\"But yours is too small.\"\n\nShe looked at him in surprise.\n\n\"I noticed yesterday.\"\n\n\"It's starting to rain more often.\"\n\n\"So...\"\n\nHe pushed the umbrella gently toward her.\n\n\"...I'd worry less if you had this.\"\n\nFor a moment...\n\nYoon-ah forgot how to breathe.\n\nAcross the room...\n\nMin-seo watched quietly.\n\nShe smiled.\n\nBut this time...\n\nit didn't quite reach her eyes.\n\n\nThat night...\n\nJae-hyun found himself thinking about something his grandmother used to say.\n\n\"When someone's safety becomes your habit...\n\nyour heart may already know something your mind hasn't accepted.\"\n\nHe closed his eyes.\n\nThen laughed softly to himself.\n\n\"No...\"\n\nhe whispered.\n\n\"It couldn't be.\"\n\nYet...\n\nhis heart never argued back.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n“Love rarely arrives all at once.\n\nSometimes... it begins with simply wanting someone to get home safely.”"
