      "number": 18,
      "content": "🌸Chapter 18\nThe Day She Didn't Come\n\nOpening Quote\n\n\"Sometimes the loudest silence...\n\nis created by one person not showing up.\"\n\nThe library felt different.\n\nJae-hyun noticed it the moment he walked through the doors.\n\nThe chair across from him...\n\nwas empty.\n\nHe glanced at the clock.\n\n2:14 p.m.\n\n\"She's probably running late.\"\n\nHe smiled to himself as he opened his notebook.\n\nFifteen minutes passed.\n\nThen thirty.\n\nThe chair remained empty.\n\nHe tried reading.\n\nThe same paragraph.\n\nAgain.\n\nAnd again.\n\nNone of the words stayed in his mind.\n\n\"Are you waiting for someone?\"\n\nThe librarian's voice broke the silence.\n\nJae-hyun looked up.\n\n\"What?\"\n\n\"You've checked the entrance six times already.\"\n\nHe blinked.\n\n\n\"Have I?\"\n\nThe librarian smiled knowingly.\n\n\"I think so.\"\n\nBy the time the library closed...\n\nYoon-ah still hadn't arrived.\n\nThe next day...\n\nHer seat was empty again.\n\nMin-seo placed her bag on the table.\n\n\"Is Yoon-ah absent today too?\"\n\n\"I guess.\"\n\nJae-hyun answered quietly.\n\n\"That's unusual.\"\n\nHe nodded.\n\n\"She never misses our study sessions.\"\n\nThe words slipped out before he realized what he'd said.\n\nOur study sessions.\n\nNot his.\n\nNot hers.\n\nOurs.\n\nThat evening...\n\nRain tapped gently against Yoon-ah's bedroom window.\n\nShe sat at her desk, staring at the unfinished letter in front of her.\n\nShe hadn't gone to the library for two days.\n\nNot because she was sick.\n\nBecause she was afraid.\n\nAfraid that every kind gesture from Jae-hyun would make it harder to accept the truth.\n\nShe had seen the way Min-seo looked at him.\n\n\nShe had seen the way he smiled back.\n\nMaybe...\n\nShe thought.\n\nMaybe stepping away was the kindest thing she could do.\n\nShe folded the unfinished letter.\n\nThen placed it inside a wooden box beneath her bed.\n\n\"I should stop.\"\n\nShe whispered the words aloud.\n\nAs if hearing them would make them true.\n\nOn the third afternoon...\n\nJae-hyun walked into the library carrying two cups of coffee.\n\nHe stopped.\n\nOne cup suddenly felt unnecessary.\n\nHe looked at the empty chair.\n\nWithout thinking...\n\nHe placed the second cup in front of it anyway.\n\nMin-seo arrived a few minutes later.\n\nShe smiled when she saw him.\n\nThen noticed the untouched coffee.\n\n\"You bought two?\"\n\nHe looked down.\n\n\"I guess...\"\n\nHe smiled awkwardly.\n\n\"I forgot.\"\n\nBut deep inside...\n\nHe knew he hadn't forgotten.\n\nHe had expected someone.\n\n\nAs the hours passed...\n\nThe coffee slowly grew cold.\n\nExactly where he had placed it.\n\nExactly where Yoon-ah should have been sitting.\n\nThat evening...\n\nJae-hyun stood outside the library.\n\nThe winter wind brushed against his face.\n\nHe reached into his pocket.\n\nThere, folded carefully...\n\nwas the small receipt from the umbrella he had bought for Yoon-ah.\n\nHe had almost thrown it away.\n\nFor some reason...\n\nHe couldn't.\n\nHe looked toward the road she always walked home on.\n\nEmpty.\n\nQuiet.\n\nFor the first time since they met...\n\nHe wished she would appear.\n\nEven if only to say goodbye.\n\nAcross town...\n\nYoon-ah stood by her bedroom window.\n\nLooking at the same evening sky.\n\nShe wondered if anyone had noticed she was gone.\n\nThen she laughed softly at herself.\n\n\"Of course not.\"\n\nSome hearts...\n\nBecome so used to loving in silence...\n\n\nThey begin to believe their absence is silent too.\n\nShe closed the curtains.\n\nUnaware...\n\nThat someone had spent three afternoons looking at an empty chair.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n\"You don't always realize someone's place in your life...\n\nuntil you're forced to imagine the day without them.\""
