      "number": 21,
      "content": "🌸Chapter 21\nThe Winter Festival\n\nOpening Quote\n\n“Some memories aren't made because life is perfect.\n\nThey're made because, for one brief moment... happiness feels enough.”\n\nThe campus transformed overnight.\n\nColorful lights hung from the trees.\n\nSmall wooden stalls lined the walkways.\n\nThe smell of roasted chestnuts and sweet pastries filled the cold air.\n\nStudents laughed as music echoed through the university courtyard.\n\nThe annual Winter Festival had begun.\n\nYoon-ah stopped near the entrance.\n\nShe had almost turned around twice before coming.\n\nCrowds had never been her favorite.\n\nToo many voices.\n\nToo many strangers.\n\nToo many chances to feel invisible.\n\n\"Yoon-ah!\"\n\nShe turned.\n\nJae-hyun waved from across the courtyard.\n\nFor some reason...\n\nSeeing him made the noise around her disappear.\n\n\"You actually came.\"\n\nHe smiled.\n\n\"I wasn't sure you would.\"\n\n\"I almost didn't.\"\n\n\"I'm glad you changed your mind.\"\n\n\nThey wandered through the festival together.\n\nStopping at different stalls.\n\nTrying games neither of them were good at.\n\nLaughing whenever they lost.\n\nFor a little while...\n\nLife felt wonderfully ordinary.\n\nAt one booth...\n\nA small basket sat beside a handwritten sign.\n\nWrite a wish.\n\nHang it on the Winter Tree.\n\nYoon-ah picked up one of the paper tags.\n\n\"What are you going to wish for?\"\n\nJae-hyun asked.\n\n\"If I tell you...\"\n\nShe smiled.\n\n\"It won't come true.\"\n\nHe laughed.\n\n\"Fair enough.\"\n\nThey stood several steps apart.\n\nEach quietly writing.\n\nYoon-ah stared at the blank paper for a long time.\n\nThen she wrote:\n\nI hope the people I love find happiness...\n\nEven if I'm not part of it.\n\nShe folded the tag quickly.\n\nBefore anyone could read it.\n\nJae-hyun finished writing much faster.\n\n\nHe tied his tag to one of the higher branches.\n\n\"What did you wish for?\"\n\nShe asked.\n\nHe smiled.\n\n\"I can't tell you.\"\n\n\"Then it won't come true?\"\n\n\"Exactly.\"\n\nNeither of them realized...\n\nThe wind had loosened one of the ribbons.\n\nYoon-ah's wish drifted gently to the ground.\n\nA little girl picked it up.\n\nShe looked around.\n\n\"Excuse me!\"\n\nShe called.\n\n\"I think someone dropped this.\"\n\nJae-hyun turned instinctively.\n\nBefore the little girl could hand it to him...\n\nYoon-ah hurried over.\n\n\"It's mine.\"\n\nShe accepted it with a grateful smile.\n\nHer hands trembled ever so slightly.\n\n\"You almost lost your wish.\"\n\nJae-hyun said.\n\nShe looked down at the folded paper.\n\nSome wishes...\n\nWere never meant to be read.\n\nAs evening approached...\n\n\nSnow began falling once again.\n\nThe festival lights reflected softly against the white ground.\n\nEverything looked like a dream.\n\n\"Come on.\"\n\nJae-hyun said.\n\n\"I want to show you something.\"\n\nHe led her toward the center of campus.\n\nA massive tree stood there.\n\nCovered in thousands of tiny lights.\n\nStudents gathered beneath it.\n\nLooking up in silence.\n\n\"It's beautiful.\"\n\nYoon-ah whispered.\n\n\"It is.\"\n\nJae-hyun answered.\n\nBut...\n\nHe wasn't looking at the tree.\n\nHe was looking at her.\n\nThe lights danced in her eyes.\n\nSnow rested gently in her hair.\n\nWithout realizing it...\n\nHe smiled.\n\nFrom the other side of the courtyard...\n\nMin-seo watched them.\n\nShe had arrived only moments earlier.\n\nShe hadn't planned on interrupting.\n\nShe simply stood there.\n\n\nQuietly.\n\nWatching two people who didn't yet understand what was happening between them.\n\nHer smile slowly faded.\n\nNot because she was angry.\n\nBecause...\n\nFor the first time...\n\nShe realized she might already know how this story would end.\n\nAnd she wasn't sure she was ready for it.\n\nThat night...\n\nYoon-ah opened her notebook.\n\nShe didn't write a letter.\n\nInstead...\n\nShe wrote one simple sentence.\n\nToday, I laughed without pretending.\n\nShe smiled.\n\nClosed the notebook.\n\nAnd for the first time in weeks...\n\nShe fell asleep without tears.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n“The happiest moments often arrive quietly...\n\nOnly later do we realize they became memories.”"
