      "content": "🌸Chapter 23\nThe Borrowed Book\n\nOpening Quote\n\n“Some stories don't change your life because they're extraordinary.\n\nThey change your life because of who was beside you while you read them.”\n\nWinter settled gently over the campus.\n\nThe library was quieter than usual.\n\nMost students were preparing for their final exams.\n\nThe familiar table by the window had become more than a place to study.\n\nIt had become a habit.\n\nJae-hyun arrived first.\n\nAs always...\n\n2:14 p.m.\n\nHe smiled when he saw the chair across from him.\n\nHe no longer thought of it as an empty seat.\n\nIn his mind...\n\nIt already belonged to Yoon-ah.\n\nA few moments later...\n\nShe walked in carrying two books against her chest.\n\n\"Am I late?\"\n\nHe looked at the clock.\n\n\"Two minutes.\"\n\nShe laughed softly.\n\n\"I'll try harder tomorrow.\"\n\n\"You don't have to.\"\n\nHe smiled.\n\n\"I don't mind waiting.\"\n\n\nThe words escaped so naturally...\n\nNeither of them realized how much they meant.\n\nAs they studied...\n\nJae-hyun reached for a novel from the library shelf.\n\n\"I've heard this one is good.\"\n\nYoon-ah's eyes brightened.\n\n\"I've read it.\"\n\n\"You have?\"\n\nShe nodded.\n\n\"It made me cry.\"\n\nHe raised an eyebrow.\n\n\"That sounds like a recommendation.\"\n\n\"It is.\"\n\nHe checked the book out.\n\nThen held it up.\n\n\"When I finish...\"\n\n\"I'll tell you what I think.\"\n\n\"I'll be waiting.\"\n\nThe next afternoon...\n\nHe returned carrying the novel.\n\n\"I finished it.\"\n\n\"So?\"\n\nShe smiled.\n\nHe looked at the cover for a long moment.\n\n\"I understand why you cried.\"\n\n\"You do?\"\n\n\"It wasn't the ending.\"\n\n\nHe closed the book gently.\n\n\"It was realizing how much the characters loved each other before either of them admitted it.\"\n\nYoon-ah's heart skipped.\n\nShe looked away.\n\n\"So...\"\n\n\"What would you have changed?\"\n\nHe asked.\n\nShe thought carefully.\n\n\"Nothing.\"\n\n\"Really?\"\n\nShe nodded.\n\n\"Not every love story needs a perfect ending.\"\n\n\"Sometimes...\"\n\n\"The love itself is enough.\"\n\nJae-hyun looked at her quietly.\n\nThere was something about the way she said those words.\n\nAs though...\n\nShe believed them.\n\nNot because she had read them.\n\nBecause she had lived them.\n\nWhen they stood to leave...\n\nHe noticed something tucked inside the last page of the novel.\n\nA small handwritten note.\n\nNot a letter.\n\nJust a quote.\n\n\"Every book returns to the shelf.\n\nSome feelings never do.\"\n\n\n\"There wasn't a note in here yesterday.\"\n\nHe murmured.\n\nYoon-ah looked surprised.\n\n\"I didn't put it there.\"\n\nThe librarian smiled from across the room.\n\n\"I did.\"\n\nThey both turned.\n\nHe chuckled.\n\n\"You two talk about books every afternoon.\"\n\n\"I thought that novel deserved one more sentence.\"\n\nThe three of them laughed together.\n\nThe moment was small.\n\nOrdinary.\n\nYet somehow...\n\nIt became one of those memories neither of them would ever forget.\n\nThat evening...\n\nJae-hyun placed the borrowed novel on his desk.\n\nInstead of returning it to the shelf immediately...\n\nHe opened it again.\n\nHe reread several pages.\n\nNot because he had forgotten the story.\n\nBut because...\n\nIt reminded him of someone.\n\nAcross the city...\n\nYoon-ah opened her notebook.\n\nShe didn't write a letter.\n\nInstead...\n\n\nShe wrote a single line.\n\nSome days become chapters you'll carry long after the book is closed.\n\nShe smiled.\n\nClosed the notebook.\n\nAnd quietly looked forward to tomorrow.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n“The right person can turn an ordinary afternoon...\n\ninto one of your favorite memories.”"
