      "content": "🌸Chapter 25\nA Simple Question\n\nOpening Quote\n\n“Sometimes... one question is enough to change everything.\n\nEspecially when your heart isn't ready to answer it.”\n\nThe library was unusually lively that afternoon.\n\nFinal exams were only a week away.\n\nEvery table was occupied.\n\nPens scratched across notebooks.\n\nPages turned one after another.\n\nThe quiet room carried the familiar rhythm of students chasing deadlines.\n\nYoon-ah arrived a few minutes early.\n\nShe smiled when she noticed a cup of warm tea waiting on the table.\n\nA small note rested beneath it.\n\nYou looked cold yesterday.\n\n–J\n\nShe couldn't help but smile.\n\nThe note was simple.\n\nYet it warmed her more than the tea.\n\nShe carefully slipped it inside her notebook.\n\nAnother little memory she couldn't bear to throw away.\n\nAt exactly 2:14 p.m...\n\nJae-hyun walked in.\n\nHe looked relieved when he saw her.\n\n\"I was worried the tea would get cold.\"\n\nShe laughed softly.\n\n\"It didn't.\"\n\n\n\"Good.\"\n\nFor some reason...\n\nThat one word made both of them smile.\n\nThey spent the afternoon studying side by side.\n\nEvery now and then...\n\nOne of them would explain a difficult topic.\n\nThe other would listen patiently.\n\nWithout realizing it...\n\nThey had become each other's favorite study partner.\n\nAs they packed their bags...\n\nThe librarian approached with a stack of returned books.\n\nHe placed them on the trolley.\n\nThen looked at the two of them.\n\n\"I've been wondering something.\"\n\nJae-hyun looked up.\n\n\"What is it?\"\n\nThe librarian smiled.\n\n\"How long have you two been together?\"\n\nSilence.\n\nComplete silence.\n\nYoon-ah nearly dropped the book in her hands.\n\nJae-hyun blinked.\n\n\"What?\"\n\nThe librarian chuckled.\n\n\"I assumed you were a couple.\"\n\n\"You always arrive together.\"\n\n\"Study together.\"\n\n\n\"Leave together.\"\n\n\"And somehow...\"\n\nHe smiled warmly.\n\n\"You both seem happiest when the other is here.\"\n\nYoon-ah quickly looked down.\n\nShe could feel her cheeks burning.\n\n\"No...\"\n\nShe whispered.\n\n\"We're just friends.\"\n\nThe words were gentle.\n\nBut saying them hurt more than she expected.\n\nThe librarian nodded kindly.\n\n\"I see.\"\n\nHe didn't say another word.\n\nHe simply smiled and returned to his work.\n\nThe walk home felt different.\n\nNeither of them spoke for several minutes.\n\nFinally...\n\nJae-hyun broke the silence.\n\n\"People make funny assumptions.\"\n\nYoon-ah forced a small smile.\n\n\"They do.\"\n\nAnother silence followed.\n\nLonger this time.\n\nNeither of them knew why the conversation had suddenly become difficult.\n\nThat night...\n\nJae-hyun lay awake staring at the ceiling.\n\n\nThe librarian's question echoed in his mind.\n\nHow long have you two been together?\n\nHe laughed quietly to himself.\n\n\"What a strange question.\"\n\nYet...\n\nInstead of dismissing it...\n\nHe found himself wondering why it had stayed with him all evening.\n\nAcross town...\n\nYoon-ah unfolded the tiny note from beneath the tea.\n\nYou looked cold yesterday.\n\n–J\n\nShe traced the letter J with her fingertip.\n\nThen carefully placed the note inside the wooden box beneath her bed.\n\nShe whispered softly,\n\n\"Friends...\"\n\nThe word lingered in the quiet room.\n\nIt sounded safe.\n\nIt sounded reasonable.\n\nBut somehow...\n\nIt didn't sound like the whole truth anymore.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n“Sometimes the hardest words to hear...\n\nare the ones you've been telling yourself all along.”"
