      "number": 26,
      "content": "🌸Chapter 26\nThe Letter That Wasn't Meant to Be Found\n\nOpening Quote\n\n“Not every secret is hidden because it's shameful.\n\nSome are hidden because the truth feels too fragile.”\n\nThe morning began with rain.\n\nNot the heavy kind.\n\nJust a quiet drizzle that covered the campus in silver.\n\nBy afternoon...\n\nThe library windows were dotted with tiny raindrops.\n\nInside, everything felt calm.\n\nYoon-ah arrived carrying a canvas tote bag instead of her usual backpack.\n\n\"It got wet this morning,\" she explained with a laugh.\n\nJae-hyun smiled.\n\n\"I like this one.\"\n\n\"It's older.\"\n\n\"So?\"\n\n\"It looks like it's been on a lot of adventures.\"\n\nShe looked down at the worn fabric.\n\n\"Maybe it has.\"\n\nThey spent the next few hours studying.\n\nTime passed the way it always did with them.\n\nQuietly.\n\nComfortably.\n\nWithout either of them noticing.\n\nAs the library announced its closing time...\n\nYoon-ah packed her books in a hurry.\n\n\n\"I promised my mother I'd be home early.\"\n\n\"You should go.\"\n\n\"I'll return these.\"\n\nJae-hyun lifted the stack of books from the table.\n\n\"Thank you.\"\n\nShe smiled.\n\nThen hurried toward the exit.\n\nA few minutes later...\n\nJae-hyun noticed something still resting beneath her chair.\n\nHer notebook.\n\nHe picked it up.\n\n\"I'll give it to her tomorrow.\"\n\nAs he lifted it...\n\nA folded piece of paper slipped onto the floor.\n\nHe instinctively bent down and picked it up.\n\nHe didn't mean to open it.\n\nIn fact...\n\nHe was about to tuck it back inside.\n\nThen he noticed the first line.\n\nDear...\n\nHe froze.\n\nIt looked like the beginning of a letter.\n\nHe hesitated.\n\nHis grandmother had always taught him not to read things that weren't his.\n\nHe carefully folded it again.\n\nWithout reading another word.\n\nHe slipped it back inside the notebook exactly as he had found it.\n\n\nThe next afternoon...\n\nYoon-ah arrived looking worried.\n\n\"My notebook...\"\n\nJae-hyun held it up with a smile.\n\n\"You left it yesterday.\"\n\nRelief washed across her face.\n\n\"You found it.\"\n\n\"I did.\"\n\nShe hugged the notebook tightly against her chest.\n\n\"Thank you.\"\n\n\"There was a paper inside.\"\n\nHe added gently.\n\n\"It fell out.\"\n\n\"I put it back.\"\n\nShe looked at him, surprised.\n\n\"You... didn't read it?\"\n\nHe shook his head.\n\n\"It wasn't mine.\"\n\nFor a moment...\n\nNeither of them spoke.\n\nThen Yoon-ah smiled.\n\nNot because he had returned her notebook.\n\nBecause he had respected her silence.\n\nThat afternoon...\n\nStudying was difficult.\n\nNot because of the exams.\n\nBut because every time Yoon-ah looked at him...\n\n\nShe remembered the folded letter hidden inside her notebook.\n\nThe one that began with:\n\nDear Jae-hyun...\n\nHe had been one decision away from reading it.\n\nOne moment.\n\nOne choice.\n\nYet...\n\nHe had chosen trust instead.\n\nAs they left the library...\n\nThe rain had stopped.\n\nThe clouds slowly drifted apart.\n\nSunlight broke through for the first time all day.\n\nJae-hyun looked up.\n\n\"I almost forgot what blue skies looked like.\"\n\nYoon-ah laughed.\n\n\"They were always there.\"\n\n\"We just couldn't see them.\"\n\nHe looked at her for a second.\n\n\"Maybe that's true about a lot of things.\"\n\nShe wondered if he meant more than the weather.\n\nShe didn't ask.\n\nThat night...\n\nYoon-ah unfolded the letter in her room.\n\nShe read the first line.\n\nDear Jae-hyun...\n\nThen, after a long silence...\n\nShe folded it again.\n\n\nPlaced it back inside the notebook.\n\nAnd whispered,\n\n\"Not yet.\"\n\nEnding Quote\n\n“Trust isn't always shown by what someone says.\n\nSometimes... it's shown by the pages they choose not to read.”"
