      "content": "🌸Chapter 35\nWhen I Started Looking for You\n\nOpening Quote\n\n\"Love rarely begins on the day you notice it.\n\nIt begins on the ordinary days you never thought to remember.\"\n\nMonday arrived with clear blue skies.\n\nThe cherry blossoms still covered the campus.\n\nThough each day...\n\nA few more petals disappeared into the wind.\n\nJae-hyun reached the library early.\n\n2:05 p.m.\n\nHe placed his backpack beside the chair.\n\nThen looked toward the entrance.\n\nWithout realizing it...\n\nHe smiled.\n\n\"You seem happy today.\"\n\nThe librarian said while arranging returned books.\n\nJae-hyun laughed.\n\n\"Do I?\"\n\n\"You've looked at the door three times.\"\n\n\"I have?\"\n\n\"You have.\"\n\nHe looked down, embarrassed.\n\n\"I guess I'm waiting for someone.\"\n\nThe librarian simply smiled.\n\n\"I know.\"\n\nA few moments later...\n\n\nThe library doors opened.\n\nYoon-ah stepped inside, slightly out of breath.\n\n\"I'm sorry.\"\n\n\"I almost missed the bus.\"\n\nJae-hyun smiled.\n\n\"You made it.\"\n\nSomehow...\n\nThose three words sounded warmer than they ever had before.\n\nThe afternoon passed quietly.\n\nHalfway through their study session...\n\nYoon-ah noticed him staring out the window.\n\n\"What are you thinking about?\"\n\nHe hesitated.\n\n\"Can I ask you something?\"\n\nShe nodded.\n\n\"Of course.\"\n\n\"When did we become... this close?\"\n\nShe looked surprised.\n\n\"I don't know.\"\n\n\"I've been wondering.\"\n\nHe smiled softly.\n\n\"It feels like it happened without me noticing.\"\n\nYoon-ah looked around the library.\n\nThe shelves.\n\nThe window.\n\nThe table they had shared for months.\n\n\"Maybe...\"\n\n\n\"It happened one ordinary day at a time.\"\n\nHe thought about that answer.\n\nIt sounded exactly right.\n\nAfter a while...\n\nThe librarian walked over carrying an old notebook.\n\n\"I found this while cleaning a storage room.\"\n\n\"It belonged to students years ago.\"\n\nHe opened it carefully.\n\nInside...\n\nDozens of graduates had written short messages before leaving the university.\n\nSome were funny.\n\nSome were hopeful.\n\nSome simply thanked the friends they had made.\n\n\"Would you like to add something?\"\n\nHe asked.\n\nYoon-ah looked uncertain.\n\n\"We're not graduating yet.\"\n\nThe librarian chuckled.\n\n\"Memories don't wait for graduation.\"\n\nJae-hyun picked up the pen first.\n\nHe thought quietly.\n\nThen wrote:\n\nSome afternoons quietly become the happiest part of your life.\n\nHe closed the notebook and handed it to Yoon-ah.\n\nShe stared at the blank page for a long moment.\n\nThen wrote beneath his words:\n\nThe people beside you are what make those afternoons unforgettable.\n\n\nShe closed the notebook gently.\n\nNeither of them read what the other had written.\n\nNot yet.\n\nAs they prepared to leave...\n\nA breeze drifted through the open window.\n\nThe notebook's pages fluttered.\n\nThe librarian caught it before it fell.\n\nHe smiled as he glanced at the two messages.\n\nHe didn't say a word.\n\nSome thoughts...\n\nWere too precious to interrupt.\n\nOutside...\n\nThe afternoon sun painted long shadows across the campus.\n\nStudents laughed beneath the cherry blossoms.\n\nJae-hyun and Yoon-ah walked side by side.\n\nNeither of them noticed how naturally their steps matched.\n\nAt the campus gate...\n\nThey stopped.\n\n\"I'll see you tomorrow.\"\n\nYoon-ah said.\n\nJae-hyun nodded.\n\n\"Tomorrow.\"\n\nShe walked toward the bus stop.\n\nHe remained where he was.\n\nWatching until she disappeared around the corner.\n\nOnly then did he turn to leave.\n\nThat evening...\n\n\nJae-hyun sat at his desk.\n\nHis eyes wandered to the cherry blossom photograph pinned above it.\n\nThen to the bookmark.\n\nThen to the library card resting beside his books.\n\nEvery one of those memories had something in common.\n\nYoon-ah.\n\nHe leaned back in his chair.\n\nA quiet smile spread across his face.\n\nThen, almost in disbelief...\n\nHe whispered,\n\n\"When did I start looking for you... before I looked for anyone else?\"\n\nNo one answered.\n\nHe didn't need an answer anymore.\n\nHis heart already had one.\n\nEnding Quote\n\n“The heart doesn't always announce when it falls in love...\n\nSometimes, it simply begins waiting for one person every day.”"
