      "content": "🌸Chapter 48\nA Place Reserved for You\n\nOpening Quote\n\n“Love doesn't always change the world around you.\n\nSometimes... it simply changes the way you walk through it.”\n\nThe days that followed felt surprisingly ordinary.\n\nThe library still opened at the same time.\n\nThe old clock still ticked above the entrance.\n\nThe librarian still greeted every student with the same warm smile.\n\nNothing had changed.\n\nExcept...\n\nEverything had.\n\nYoon-ah no longer wondered whether Jae-hyun would come.\n\nShe knew he would.\n\nAnd somehow...\n\nThat certainty made every afternoon feel peaceful.\n\nOne rainy afternoon...\n\nShe arrived a little later than usual.\n\nThe library was almost full.\n\nStudents had taken nearly every seat.\n\nShe looked around.\n\nThen smiled.\n\nThe chair by the window—\n\nThe one across from Jae-hyun—\n\nWas still empty.\n\n\"You saved it.\"\n\nShe said quietly.\n\n\nJae-hyun looked up from his book.\n\n\"I always do.\"\n\nShe sat down.\n\nNeither of them mentioned it again.\n\nSome things no longer needed explaining.\n\nOutside...\n\nRain tapped softly against the windows.\n\nInside...\n\nThe world smelled of paper, coffee, and old wood.\n\n\"What are you reading?\"\n\nYoon-ah asked.\n\nJae-hyun turned the book toward her.\n\n\"It's the novel we almost borrowed on the first day we met.\"\n\nHer eyes widened.\n\n\"You remembered?\"\n\nHe laughed softly.\n\n\"I remember more than you think.\"\n\nShe opened the first page.\n\nInside the cover...\n\nSomeone had written years before:\n\nTo the person who finds this book—may you discover a story worth keeping.\n\nShe smiled.\n\n\"I think we already did.\"\n\nHe looked at her.\n\n\"I think so too.\"\n\nThe afternoon passed in comfortable silence.\n\nEvery now and then...\n\n\nTheir hands brushed as they reached for the same page.\n\nNeither of them pulled away immediately.\n\nNeither hurried the moment.\n\nWhen evening came...\n\nThe librarian approached with two steaming cups.\n\n\"I thought today called for hot chocolate.\"\n\nJae-hyun laughed.\n\n\"You remembered too.\"\n\nThe old man smiled.\n\n\"I'm old.\"\n\n\"Not forgetful.\"\n\nThe three of them laughed together.\n\nAs they prepared to leave...\n\nThe librarian stopped them.\n\n\"I have something for you.\"\n\nFrom behind the desk...\n\nHe brought out a small wooden plaque.\n\nIts edges were worn smooth with age.\n\nHe placed it gently on the table by the window.\n\nCarved into it were the words:\n\nReserved for Quiet Readers\n\nHe looked at them with a smile.\n\n\"I've been thinking...\"\n\n\"I don't think this table belongs to the library anymore.\"\n\nThey looked at him, confused.\n\nHe chuckled.\n\n\"I think it belongs to the memories you've made here.\"\n\n\nYoon-ah's eyes filled with tears.\n\nJae-hyun bowed respectfully.\n\n\"Thank you.\"\n\nBefore leaving...\n\nYoon-ah gently ran her fingers across the edge of the table.\n\n\"This place...\"\n\nShe whispered.\n\n\"...gave me more than books.\"\n\nJae-hyun looked at her.\n\n\"It gave me home.\"\n\nThey walked out together.\n\nThe rain had stopped.\n\nThe sky glowed with the soft colors of sunset.\n\nFor the first time...\n\nNeither of them worried about tomorrow.\n\nBecause tomorrow...\n\nWould be another ordinary afternoon.\n\nTogether.\n\nThat evening...\n\nYoon-ah opened the wooden box beneath her bed one last time.\n\nInside were:\n\nThe first bookmark.\n\nThe tiny note reminding her to rest.\n\nThe cherry blossom photograph.\n\nThe silver bookmark.\n\nAnd Jae-hyun's letter.\n\nShe smiled.\n\n\nThen carefully closed the lid.\n\nShe no longer needed to hide those memories.\n\nFrom now on...\n\nShe would be making new ones with him.\n\nAcross town...\n\nJae-hyun placed her letter inside his favorite book.\n\nNot to forget it.\n\nBut because...\n\nSome stories deserved to stay close to the heart that cherished them.\n\nHe looked out his window.\n\nSmiled.\n\nAnd whispered,\n\n\"See you tomorrow.\"\n\nEnding Quote\n\n“The greatest gift love gave them wasn't a perfect ending...\n\nIt was the promise of another ordinary tomorrow.”"
