  "backMatter": "Acknowledgements\nWriting this story has been a journey filled with quiet moments, hope, and imagination.\n\nThank you to every reader who chose to spend time within these pages. Every chapter was written\nwith care, and I hope you found a piece of yourself somewhere between the library shelves, the\nfalling cherry blossoms, and the silence shared by two hearts.\n\nMay this story remind you that love doesn't always arrive with grand gestures. Sometimes, it begins\nwith kindness, grows through patience, and stays with us in the smallest moments.\n\nThank you for reading.\n\nWith gratitude,\n\nBlessing Effiong\n\n\n🌸About the Author\nBlessing Effiong is a storyteller who enjoys writing gentle, emotional romances that celebrate quiet\nmoments, meaningful connections, and the beauty found in everyday life.\n\nA Love Written in Silence is her debut novel, inspired by the idea that the most unforgettable love\nstories are often the quietest ones.\n\nWhen she isn't writing, Blessing enjoys learning new skills, reading, exploring forex trading, creating\ndigital content, and finding inspiration for the next story waiting to be told.\n\n\n💌Thank You for Reading\nIf you've reached this page...\n\nThank you.\n\nThank you for giving your time, your heart, and your imagination to this story.\n\nI hope Yoon-ah and Jae-hyun's journey reminded you that love isn't always loud. Sometimes it grows\nin shared silences, kind gestures, and ordinary afternoons that quietly become unforgettable\nmemories.\n\nIf this story made you smile, cry, or simply pause for a moment, then it has found the home it was\nmeant to find.\n\nUntil we meet again in another story...\n\nTake care of your heart.\n\nWith love,\n\nBlessing Effiong\n\n\"Every time you walk into a library, look for the seat by the window. You never know where your next beautiful story might\nbegin.\""
